  "final_text": "You had **108 accounts with status `A`** on 30 June. If `N` also counts as active, the figure is **132**. The export has no key for the status codes, so I can't tell which one you mean.\n\n| Status | Count | Status dates |\n|---|---|---|\n| `A` | 108 | 2025-01-02 → 2026-03-20 |\n| `C` | 12 | 2026-04-05 → 2026-06-24 |\n| `N` | 24 | 2026-04-03 → 2026-06-20 |\n| **Total** | **144** | |\n\n**Why the answer depends on `N`:** No `A` record has a date after 20 March 2026, and every `N` record starts on or after 3 April. That pattern suggests `N` means \"New\": accounts added since April that are probably live but still have a separate status. `C` looks like churned or cancelled, so I left those out either way. If `N` actually means something like \"non-renewing\" or \"inactive,\" the answer is 108. If it means new, live customers, it's 132.\n\n**Is this snapshot right for 30 June?** The file only stores each account's current status, not its history. The latest status date is 24 June, so nothing changed between 30 June and when the file was exported. That means today's statuses are the same as the 30 June statuses.\n\nWhat does `N` mean in your system? I'll confirm whichever number fits.",
